#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Qiskit SDK provides some tools for converting between OpenQASM representations of quantum programs, and the [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) class.\n"
msgstr "Qiskit SDK menyediakan beberapa alat untuk menukar antara representasi OpenQASM program kuantum, dan kelas [QuantumCircuit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qasm2-import\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"qasm2-import\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Import an OpenQASM 2 program into Qiskit {#import-an-openqasm-2-program-into-qiskit}"
msgstr "Import program OpenQASM 2 ke dalam Qiskit {#import-an-openqasm-2-program-into-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two functions import OpenQASM 2 programs into Qiskit.\n"
"These are [`qasm2.load()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#load), which takes a filename, and [`qasm2.loads()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#loads), which takes the OpenQASM 2 program as a string.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua fungsi mengimport program OpenQASM 2 ke dalam Qiskit.\n"
"Ini ialah [`qasm2.load()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#load), yang mengambil nama fail, dan [`qasm2.loads()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#loads), yang mengambil program OpenQASM 2 sebagai rentetan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See the [OpenQASM 2 Qiskit API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qasm2) for more information.\n"
msgstr "Lihat [OpenQASM 2 Qiskit API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qasm2) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Import simple programs {#import-simple-programs}"
msgstr "Import program mudah {#import-simple-programs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For most OpenQASM 2 programs, you can simply use `qasm2.load` and `qasm2.loads` with a single argument.\n"
msgstr "Untuk kebanyakan program OpenQASM 2, anda boleh menggunakan `qasm2.load` dan `qasm2.loads` dengan hujah tunggal.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: import an OpenQASM 2 program as a string {#example-import-an-openqasm-2-program-as-a-string}"
msgstr "Contoh: import program OpenQASM 2 sebagai rentetan {#example-import-an-openqasm-2-program-as-a-string}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `qasm2.loads()` to import an OpenQASM 2 program as a string into a QuantumCircuit:\n"
msgstr "Gunakan `qasm2.loads()` untuk mengimport program OpenQASM 2 sebagai rentetan ke dalam QuantumCircuit:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: import an OpenQASM 2 program from a file {#example-import-an-openqasm-2-program-from-a-file}"
msgstr "Contoh: import program OpenQASM 2 dari fail {#example-import-an-openqasm-2-program-from-a-file}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use `load()` to import an OpenQASM 2 program from a file into a QuantumCircuit:\n"
msgstr "Gunakan `load()` untuk mengimport program OpenQASM 2 dari fail ke dalam QuantumCircuit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"custom-instructions\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"custom-instructions\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Link OpenQASM 2 gates with Qiskit gates {#link-openqasm-2-gates-with-qiskit-gates}"
msgstr "Hubungkan gate OpenQASM 2 dengan gate Qiskit {#link-openqasm-2-gates-with-qiskit-gates}"

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, Qiskit's OpenQASM 2 importer treats the include file `\"qelib1.inc\"` as a *de facto* standard library.\n"
"The importer treats this file as containing precisely the gates it is described to contain in [the original paper defining OpenQASM 2](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03429).\n"
"Qiskit will use the built-in gates in [the circuit library](../api/qiskit/circuit_library) to represent the gates in `\"qelib1.inc\"`.\n"
"Gates defined in the program by manual OpenQASM 2 `gate` statements will, by default, be constructed as custom [Qiskit `Gate` subclasses](../api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.Gate).\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: emptied 2026-09-05, previous translation failed check.py
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can tell the importer to use specific [`Gate`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.Gate) classes for the given `gate` statements it encounters.\n"
"You can also use this mechanism to treat additional gate names as \"built-in\", that is, not requiring an explicit definition.\n"
"If you specify which gate classes to use for `gate` statements outside of `\"qelib1.inc\"`, the resulting circuit will typically be more efficient to work with.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"warning\">\n"
"As of Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit's OpenQASM 2 *exporter* (see [Export a Qiskit circuit to OpenQASM 2](#qasm2-export)) still behaves as if `\"qelib1.inc\"` has more gates than it really does.\n"
"This means that the default settings of the importer might not be able to import a program exported by our importer.\n"
"See [the specific example on working with the legacy exporter](#qasm2-import-legacy) to resolve this problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"warning\">\n"
"Mulai Qiskit SDK v1.0, *pengeksport* OpenQASM 2 Qiskit (lihat [Eksport Circuit Qiskit ke OpenQASM 2](#qasm2-export)) masih berkelakuan seolah-olah `\"qelib1.inc\"` mempunyai lebih banyak gate daripada yang sebenarnya.\n"
"Ini bermakna tetapan lalai pengimport mungkin tidak dapat mengimport program yang dieksport oleh pengeksport kami.\n"
"Lihat [contoh khusus tentang bekerja dengan pengeksport warisan](#qasm2-import-legacy) untuk menyelesaikan masalah ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This discrepancy is legacy behavior of Qiskit, and [it will be resolved in a later release of Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/10737).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Perbezaan ini ialah tingkah laku warisan Qiskit, dan [ia akan diselesaikan dalam keluaran Qiskit kemudian](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/10737).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To pass information about a custom instruction to the OpenQASM 2 importer, use [the `qasm2.CustomInstruction` class](../api/qiskit/qasm2#qiskit.qasm2.CustomInstruction).\n"
"This has four required pieces of information, in order:\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menghantar maklumat tentang arahan tersuai kepada pengimport OpenQASM 2, gunakan [kelas `qasm2.CustomInstruction`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#qiskit.qasm2.CustomInstruction).\n"
"Ini mempunyai empat maklumat yang diperlukan, mengikut urutan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **name** of the gate, used in the OpenQASM 2 program\n"
msgstr "**Nama** gate, digunakan dalam program OpenQASM 2\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **number of angle parameters** that the gate takes\n"
msgstr "**Bilangan parameter sudut** yang diambil oleh gate\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The **number of qubits** that the gate acts on\n"
msgstr "**Bilangan qubit** yang digunakan oleh gate\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Python **constructor** class or function for the gate, which takes the gate parameters (but not qubits) as individual arguments\n"
msgstr "**Kelas konstruktor** Python atau fungsi untuk gate, yang mengambil parameter gate (tetapi bukan qubit) sebagai hujah individu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the importer encounters a `gate` definition that matches a given custom instruction, it will use that custom information to reconstruct the gate object.\n"
"If a `gate` statement is encountered that matches the `name` of a custom instruction, but does not match both the number of parameters and the number of qubits, the importer will raise a [`QASM2ParseError`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#qasm2parseerror), to indicate the mismatch between the supplied information and program.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika pengimport menemui definisi `gate` yang sepadan dengan arahan tersuai yang diberikan, ia akan menggunakan maklumat tersuai itu untuk membina semula objek gate.\n"
"Jika pernyataan `gate` ditemui yang sepadan dengan `name` arahan tersuai, tetapi tidak sepadan dengan bilangan parameter dan bilangan qubit, pengimport akan menimbulkan [`QASM2ParseError`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#qasm2parseerror), untuk menunjukkan ketidakpadanan antara maklumat yang diberikan dan program.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition, a fifth argument `builtin` can be optionally set to `True` to make the gate automatically available within the OpenQASM 2 program, even if it is not explicitly defined.\n"
"If the importer does encounter an explicit `gate` definition for a built-in custom instruction, it will accept it silently.\n"
"As before, if an explicit definition of the same name is not compatible with the provided custom instruction, a [`QASM2ParseError`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#qasm2parseerror) will be raised.\n"
"This is useful for compatibility with older OpenQASM 2 exporters, and with certain other quantum platforms that treat the \"basis gates\" of their hardware as built-in instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, hujah kelima `builtin` boleh secara pilihan ditetapkan kepada `True` untuk menjadikan gate tersedia secara automatik dalam program OpenQASM 2, walaupun ia tidak ditakrifkan secara eksplisit.\n"
"Jika pengimport menemui definisi `gate` eksplisit untuk arahan tersuai terbina dalam, ia akan menerimanya secara senyap.\n"
"Seperti sebelumnya, jika definisi eksplisit dengan nama yang sama tidak serasi dengan arahan tersuai yang diberikan, [`QASM2ParseError`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#qasm2parseerror) akan ditimbulkan.\n"
"Ini berguna untuk keserasian dengan pengeksport OpenQASM 2 yang lebih lama, dan dengan platform kuantum tertentu lain yang menganggap \"gate asas\" perkakasan mereka sebagai arahan terbina dalam.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit provides a data attribute for working with OpenQASM 2 programs produced by legacy versions of [Qiskit's OpenQASM 2 exporting capabilities](#qasm2-export).\n"
"This is [`qasm2.LEGACY_CUSTOM_INSTRUCTIONS`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#legacy-compatibility), which can be given as the `custom_instructions` argument to [`qasm2.load()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#load) and [`qasm2.loads()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#loads).\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit menyediakan atribut data untuk bekerja dengan program OpenQASM 2 yang dihasilkan oleh versi warisan [keupayaan mengeksport OpenQASM 2 Qiskit](#qasm2-export).\n"
"Ini ialah [`qasm2.LEGACY_CUSTOM_INSTRUCTIONS`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#legacy-compatibility), yang boleh diberikan sebagai hujah `custom_instructions` kepada [`qasm2.load()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#load) dan [`qasm2.loads()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#loads).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qasm2-import-legacy\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"qasm2-import-legacy\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: import a program created by Qiskit's legacy exporter {#example-import-a-program-created-by-qiskits-legacy-exporter}"
msgstr "Contoh: import program yang dicipta oleh pengeksport warisan Qiskit {#example-import-a-program-created-by-qiskits-legacy-exporter}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This OpenQASM 2 program uses gates that are not in the original version of `\"qelib1.inc\"` without declaring them, but are standard gates in Qiskit's library.\n"
"You can use [`qasm2.LEGACY_CUSTOM_INSTRUCTIONS`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#legacy-compatibility) to easily tell the importer to use the same set of gates that Qiskit's OpenQASM 2 exporter previously used.\n"
msgstr ""
"Program OpenQASM 2 ini menggunakan gate yang tidak ada dalam versi asal `\"qelib1.inc\"` tanpa mendeklarasikannya, tetapi merupakan gate standard dalam pustaka Qiskit.\n"
"Anda boleh menggunakan [`qasm2.LEGACY_CUSTOM_INSTRUCTIONS`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#legacy-compatibility) untuk memberitahu pengimport dengan mudah menggunakan set gate yang sama yang pernah digunakan oleh pengeksport OpenQASM 2 Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: use a particular gate class when importing an OpenQASM 2 program {#example-use-a-particular-gate-class-when-importing-an-openqasm-2-program}"
msgstr "Contoh: gunakan kelas gate tertentu semasa mengimport program OpenQASM 2 {#example-use-a-particular-gate-class-when-importing-an-openqasm-2-program}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit cannot, in general, verify if the definition in an OpenQASM 2 `gate` statement corresponds exactly to a Qiskit standard-library gate.\n"
"Instead, Qiskit chooses a custom gate using the precise definition supplied.\n"
"This can be less efficient that using one of the built-in standard gates, or a user-defined custom gate.\n"
"You can manually define `gate` statements with particular classes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit tidak boleh, secara umum, mengesahkan sama ada definisi dalam pernyataan `gate` OpenQASM 2 sepadan tepat dengan gate pustaka standard Qiskit.\n"
"Sebaliknya, Qiskit memilih gate tersuai menggunakan definisi tepat yang diberikan.\n"
"Ini boleh kurang cekap berbanding menggunakan salah satu gate standard terbina dalam, atau gate tersuai yang ditentukan pengguna.\n"
"Anda boleh menentukan pernyataan `gate` secara manual dengan kelas tertentu.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: define a new built-in gate in an OpenQASM 2 program {#example-define-a-new-built-in-gate-in-an-openqasm-2-program}"
msgstr "Contoh: takrifkan gate terbina dalam baharu dalam program OpenQASM 2 {#example-define-a-new-built-in-gate-in-an-openqasm-2-program}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the argument `builtin=True` is set, a custom gate does not need to have an associated definition.\n"
msgstr "Jika hujah `builtin=True` ditetapkan, gate tersuai tidak perlu mempunyai definisi yang berkaitan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"custom-classical\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"custom-classical\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define custom classical functions {#define-custom-classical-functions}"
msgstr "Takrifkan fungsi klasik tersuai {#define-custom-classical-functions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"OpenQASM 2 includes some built-in classical functions to use in gate arguments.\n"
"You can extend the language with more functions by using the `custom_classical` argument to [`qasm2.load()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#load) and [`qasm2.loads()`](../api/qiskit/qasm3#loads), with the [`qasm2.CustomClassical`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#qiskit.qasm2.CustomClassical) class.\n"
msgstr ""
"OpenQASM 2 menyertakan beberapa fungsi klasik terbina dalam untuk digunakan dalam hujah gate.\n"
"Anda boleh melanjutkan bahasa dengan lebih banyak fungsi menggunakan hujah `custom_classical` kepada [`qasm2.load()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#load) dan [`qasm2.loads()`](../api/qiskit/qasm3#loads), dengan kelas [`qasm2.CustomClassical`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#qiskit.qasm2.CustomClassical).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To define a custom classical function, you must supply:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menakrifkan fungsi klasik tersuai, anda mesti memberikan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The *name* of the function as it appears in the OpenQASM 2 program\n"
msgstr "*Nama* fungsi seperti yang muncul dalam program OpenQASM 2\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of floating-point arguments it accepts\n"
msgstr "Bilangan hujah titik terapung yang diterimanya\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A callable Python object that evaluates the function\n"
msgstr "Objek Python yang boleh dipanggil yang menilai fungsi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All defined custom classical functions are treated as built-in to the OpenQASM 2 language by the importer.\n"
"There is no official way within the OpenQASM 2 language to define new functions; this is a Qiskit extension.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semua fungsi klasik tersuai yang ditakrifkan dianggap terbina dalam bahasa OpenQASM 2 oleh pengimport.\n"
"Tiada cara rasmi dalam bahasa OpenQASM 2 untuk menakrifkan fungsi baharu; ini ialah sambungan Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: use custom classical instructions {#example-use-custom-classical-instructions}"
msgstr "Contoh: gunakan arahan klasik tersuai {#example-use-custom-classical-instructions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we provide two custom classical functions.\n"
"The first is simple, and just adds one to its input.\n"
"The second is the function ``math.atan2``, which represents the mathematical operation $\\arctan(y/x)$ in a quadrant-aware manner.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kami menyediakan dua fungsi klasik tersuai.\n"
"Yang pertama mudah, dan hanya menambah satu kepada inputnya.\n"
"Yang kedua ialah fungsi ``math.atan2``, yang mewakili operasi matematik $\\arctan(y/x)$ dengan cara yang sedar kuadran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"strict\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"strict\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Strict mode {#strict-mode}"
msgstr "Mod ketat {#strict-mode}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, this parser is more relaxed than the official specification.\n"
"It allows trailing commas in parameter lists; unnecessary (empty-statement) semicolons; omission of the `OPENQASM 2.0;` version statement; and several other quality-of-life improvements without emitting any errors.\n"
"However, you can use the \"letter-of-the-spec\" mode with `strict=True`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara lalai, penghurai ini lebih santai daripada spesifikasi rasmi.\n"
"Ia membenarkan koma pelacak dalam senarai parameter; titik koma yang tidak perlu (pernyataan kosong); pengabaian pernyataan versi `OPENQASM 2.0;`; dan beberapa peningkatan kualiti kehidupan lain tanpa mengeluarkan sebarang ralat.\n"
"Walau bagaimanapun, anda boleh menggunakan mod \"mengikut huruf spesifikasi\" dengan `strict=True`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qasm2-export\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"qasm2-export\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Export a Qiskit circuit to OpenQASM 2 {#export-a-qiskit-circuit-to-openqasm-2}"
msgstr "Eksport Circuit Qiskit ke OpenQASM 2 {#export-a-qiskit-circuit-to-openqasm-2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit can also export a [`QuantumCircuit`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) to OpenQASM 2.\n"
"You use the function [`qasm2.dump()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#dump) to write to a file, and [`qasm2.dumps()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#dumps) to write to a string.\n"
"These functions currently have a very simple interface: they accept a circuit and, only in the case of [`qasm2.dump()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#dump), a location to write the output to.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit juga boleh mengeksport [`QuantumCircuit`](../api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) ke OpenQASM 2.\n"
"Anda menggunakan fungsi [`qasm2.dump()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#dump) untuk menulis ke fail, dan [`qasm2.dumps()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#dumps) untuk menulis ke rentetan.\n"
"Fungsi-fungsi ini pada masa ini mempunyai antara muka yang sangat mudah: ia menerima circuit dan, hanya dalam kes [`qasm2.dump()`](../api/qiskit/qasm2#dump), lokasi untuk menulis output.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"warning\">\n"
"Qiskit's OpenQASM 2 exporter still assumes a legacy, non-standard version of the `\"qelib1.inc\"` include file.\n"
"[This will be resolved in a later release of Qiskit](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/10737), but in the meantime, if you need to re-import an OpenQASM 2 program created with Qiskit, use [the example above for how to tell the importer about the legacy gates](#qasm2-import-legacy).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"warning\">\n"
"Pengeksport OpenQASM 2 Qiskit masih menganggap versi warisan, bukan standard fail include `\"qelib1.inc\"`.\n"
"[Ini akan diselesaikan dalam keluaran Qiskit kemudian](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit/issues/10737), tetapi sementara itu, jika anda perlu mengimport semula program OpenQASM 2 yang dicipta dengan Qiskit, gunakan [contoh di atas tentang cara memberitahu pengimport tentang gate warisan](#qasm2-import-legacy).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example: export a circuit to OpenQASM 2 {#example-export-a-circuit-to-openqasm-2}"
msgstr "Contoh: eksport circuit ke OpenQASM 2 {#example-export-a-circuit-to-openqasm-2}"

